===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|burjon|burjon, burioun|lang=enm}} "shoot, bud" from {{etyl|xno}} {{term|burjun|burjun, burgeon, burgon|lang=xno}} (compare {{etyl|fro|-}} {{term|burjon|burjon|lang=fro}} "a bud"), of {{etyl|gem}} origin, from {{etyl|frk}} *{{term||burjo|lang=frk}} "sprout" from {{proto|Germanic|burjōn|sprout", lit. "a rise|lang=en}} from {{proto|Germanic|biranan|to carry, bear|lang=en}} from {{proto|Indo-European|bhere-, *bhrē-|to bear|lang=en}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|burjan|lang=goh}} "to push up, raise", {{ang}} {{term|byrian|lang=ang}} "to come up, occur". More at {{l|en|bear}}.

